{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-022", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["raw_material_energy_cost", "capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Kaspi cement plant upgrade begins", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/Georgia-Flag-1500.jpg\" /></p><p>Georgia: A US$70m expansion of the Kaspi cement plant has begun, according to parent company Hunnewell Cement. The company said that the project will include a new clinker line and additional grinding capacity to bring total production to 2Mt/yr, from 1Mt/yr at present. The opening of the project was attended by Hunnewell Partners’ managing partner Irakli Rukhadze, Hunnewell Cement’s director David Jugashvili, ", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/20775-kaspi-cement-plant-upgrade-begins", "type": "rss"}]}
