{"id": "unknown-2026-05-18-024", "date": "2026-05-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["涉及產能"]}, "title": "Sibcem production plummets in first three months", "content": "<p><img src=\"https://www.globalcement.com/images/news/Russian-Rubles-1500.jpg\" /></p><p><strong>Russia:</strong> JSC Sibirsky Cement Holding Company (Sibcem), has reported that it produced 0.52Mt of cement in the three months to March 2026, 37.5% less than in the same period of 2025, when it made 0.83Mt/yr.</p>\n<p>Production at the Topkinsky Cement plant fell by 47.4% to 0.19Mt, while Iskitimcement saw production fall by 23% to 0.16Mt. Krasnoyarsky Cement saw a fall of 33.3% to 84,200t, Angarsky", "sources": [{"name": "global_cement", "url": "https://www.globalcement.com/news/20773-sibcem-production-plummets-in-first-three-months", "type": "rss"}]}
